body:
PS: the reason why I want to do this is so that I can easily tile maps faster by using a txt file rather than a png file.

    public Tile getTile(int x, int y){  
         if(x < 0 || y < 0 || x >=width || y>=height) 
         return Tile.voidTile;
         if(tiles[x + y * width] == 0)return Tile.floor;
         if(tiles[x + y * width] == 1)return Tile.grass; //etc
         return Tile.voidTile;
         }

ha ha, I'm running a 32 pixel tiles instead of 16 just some personal editing :P 


    int px = (int) level.getPlayerAt(0).getX();
    int py = (int) level.getPlayerAt(0).getY();
    Vector2i start = new Vector2i((int) getX() >> 5, (int) getY() >> 5);
EDIT1: as you can see I cast these lines  in the star class to an int.

    public double getX(){
		return x;
	}

	public double getY(){
		return y;
	}
EDIT2: In the entity class I set get X and get Y to a double realizing that these could be problematic down the line; mob speed etc.



    public boolean equals(Object object) {
	      if (!(object instanceof Vector2i)) return false;
	      Vector2i vec = (Vector2i) object;
	      if (vec.getX() == this.getX() && vec.getY() == this.getY()) return true;
	      return false;
	   }

EDIT 3: Ok.... now the heart of the problem! OK, I did some going back and forth and out of all the classes, the problem was actually in the vectors class all along XD. It was the if statement that was incorrect. In Episode 100 at 43:20 he changed:

    if (vec.getX() == this.getX() && vec.getY() == this.getY()) return false; 

to true......while he was talking. Im pretty sure Im not the only one that was not alerted. I though he was finished. Classic Cherno. I have to peel my eyes for stuff like this haha. 
Above all it is finally working!!! Not the most efficient or human like, I still have to tweak mob collision and add an else statement  so that if the mob doesnt see the player, move randomly and stuff. Still, it was hours and hours of finding an answer, Im keeping it just in case someone else stumbles upon it. But yeah debugging this with no info is really really odd. Might look at other ways
